Given $h$ with $a + h in [a, b]$, the theorem says there is $theta = theta(h) in (0, 1)$ such that
$
  f(a+h) = f(a) + h f'(a + theta h).
$
Unlike the affine characterization of differentiability, this statement carries no error term: for a real function on an interval, the increment is exactly a step of the derivative at an intermediate point.
